# Normalize line endings for everyone, regardless of OS or editor.
#
# Added because this repo accumulated 35 files with LF<->CRLF-only
# diffs (no real content change) from Windows editing tools (Notepad,
# a broken PowerShell -EncodedCommand session) flipping line endings.
# That noise made real changes hard to spot in `git diff` / `git status`
# and contributed to at least one real incident: seed_demo.js's actual
# content got overwritten by reset_demo.js's logic during the same kind
# of editing session, and the corruption was easy to miss inside a
# 1800+ line diff dominated by line-ending noise.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide text vs binary; `eol=lf` forces LF in the
# repository regardless of what line ending your local checkout uses,
# so `git diff` only ever shows real content changes going forward.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files some tools might otherwise try to "normalize" and corrupt.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
